# nix build output symlinks. `nix build .#<pkg>` (the documented bump check)
# drops these at the repo root; committed once by accident (073080c) where it
# invalidated the lint check's cache on every package build.
result
result-*
# `python3 -m py_compile scripts/*.py` (the syntax check before a rebuild) drops
# these next to the source; nix would otherwise see them as untracked noise.
__pycache__/
# ruff writes its own .ruff_cache/.gitignore, but runtime-state policy lives
# HERE (see the agent-state note below), not in tool-emitted exclude files.
.ruff_cache/

# Agent runtime state. These live in the tracked .gitignore (not
# .git/info/exclude) deliberately: exclude files are machine-local and don't
# survive a clone, and unignored runtime state is exactly how 144 MiB of agent
# transcripts (.pi/) once got committed by an automated `git add -A`.
#
# .claude/ is an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist: the harness grows new state files
# on its own schedule (a denylist here was reactive -- twelve entries, each
# added only after its file had already appeared), so everything is ignored
# except the paths this repo deliberately tracks. Adding a new tracked path
# means adding a `!` line, which is the failure mode we can live with: an
# unignored new file gets committed noise-free never; an unlisted tracked
# file fails loudly at `git add`.
.pi/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
